# Prefix-Cache-Aware Prompt Ordering

When building system prompts for any LLM-calling node, **static content must come first** and **dynamic content must come last**.

## Why

vLLM prefix caching reuses KV states when consecutive requests share the same token prefix. Putting per-request dynamic content (persona, domain, task frame, taxonomy) at the start of the system prompt defeats this: every request gets a different prefix and no KV reuse.

## Rule

```
SYSTEM MESSAGE
  1. Static rules (identical across ALL requests)
  2. Static trust policy
  3. Static formatting / scoring
  --- prefix boundary ---
  4. Dynamic persona / role
  5. Dynamic domain context
  6. Dynamic output directive / taxonomy
  7. Dynamic style overrides

USER MESSAGE
  1. Task description / user query
  2. Evidence / RAG chunks
  3. Planning context (tasks, constraints, deliverables)
  4. Revision context / gate feedback
```

## When adding a new node or prompt

- NEVER put `{persona}`, `{domain}`, or any per-request variable in the first line of a system prompt
- Extract the static portion into a module-level constant (e.g., `_NODE_SYSTEM_STATIC`)
- Append dynamic content at the end of the system message, or move it to the user message
- Prefer user message for per-request context (tasks, constraints) over system message
- See `docs/performance.md` "Prefix-Aware Prompt Structure" for the full convention
